.TH iron-vault-serve 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-serve \- Run the service until SIGTERM or SIGINT
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault serve\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-to\-stdout\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the service until SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.PP
In a protected installation systemd starts it as the `iron\-vault` service account, so you never run it yourself. It starts Locked: run `unlock` after each start.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-to\-stdout\fR
Write the log to stdout until an approved config names a destination, as the Docker image does. The service refuses it when stdout is the systemd journal
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
